# javascript-Assignment

Gemini said
JavaScript Assignments - Web Dev II
This repository contains the source code for two JavaScript assignments completed for the Web Dev II coursework.

Assignment 1: Smart Event Dashboard / To-Do List
This assignment focuses on core DOM manipulation and front-end interface development using HTML, CSS, and Vanilla JavaScript.

Key Features & Concepts
Dynamic DOM Manipulation: Ability to dynamically create and delete event/task cards from the interface.

Event Handling: Interactive UI elements leveraging various event listeners.

Responsive Layout: Structured and styled using modern CSS Grid and Flexbox techniques.

Role-Based Routing: User session management and conditional redirection utilizing localStorage.

Assignment 2: Async Weather Tracker
This assignment explores asynchronous JavaScript, external API integration, and the JavaScript execution context.

Key Features & Concepts
Asynchronous Data Fetching: Utilizes the Fetch API, along with async/await syntax and Promises, to retrieve real-time weather data.

Robust Error Handling: Implements comprehensive error management using both try...catch blocks and .then()/.catch() chains to handle failed network requests gracefully.

Data Persistence: Uses browser localStorage to save, manage, and display a persistent user search history.

Event Loop Analysis: Includes strategic console logging to demonstrate and analyze the behavior of the JavaScript Event Loop.

Technologies Used
HTML5

CSS3 (Grid & Flexbox)

Vanilla JavaScript (ES6+)

Web Storage API (localStorage)

Fetch API

Setup and Execution
Clone the repository to your local machine:

Bash
git clone https://github.com/yuvrajsinghsoni06-dotcom/javascript-Assignment
Navigate to the respective assignment folders.

Open the index.html files directly in your preferred web browser to run the applications. No local server or build tools are strictly required.